thor"><name><surname>Vevera</surname><given-names>J</given-names></name><name><surname>Hubbard</surname><given-names>A</given-names></name><name><surname>Vesel&#x000fd;</surname><given-names>A</given-names></name><name><surname>Papezov&#x000e1;</surname><given-names>H</given-names></name></person-group><year>2005</year><article-title>Violent behaviour in schizophrenia. Retrospective study of four independent samples from Prague, 1949 to 2000.</article-title><source>Br J Psychiatry</source><volume>187</volume><fpage>426</fpage><lpage>430</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">16260817</pub-id></mixed-citation></ref></ref-list><fn-group><fn fn-type="conflict"><p>The author has declared that no competing interests exist.</p></fn><fn fn-type="financial-disclosure"><p>No specific funding was received for this paper.</p></fn><fn fn-type="other"><p><bold>Provenance:</bold> Commissioned; not externally peer reviewed</p></fn></fn-group></back></article>